course: dictionary
lesson: 6485
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. Navy is one of them.
explain: «Mum found her a small navy suit» uses navy to describe a colour, a very dark blue. Navy blue is the full name of that colour.
explain: «Mia-Rose's mum is on a Navy ship for six months» uses Navy with a capital N to mean the armed forces that fight at sea. The ship and the months at sea are your clue.
explain: Ask yourself: is the word describing something you can see, or naming a group of people? Your answer picks the right meaning.
fact: A navy is the part of a country's armed forces that fights at sea, with ships, sailors and submarines.
fact: Navy blue is a very dark blue colour.
fact: Navy can be a noun (a navy, navies) or an adjective that describes a colour.
fact: The Royal Navy in the UK and the US Navy are two examples of navies in different countries.
fact: «Elizabeth I ruled England for 45 years, and in 1588 her navy and stormy weather defeated the Spanish Armada.»
exercise: «Mum found her a small navy suit.» What colour is the suit? | Brown | Bright red | *Very dark blue | Pale yellow
exercise: «Mia-Rose's mum is on a Navy ship for six months.» What does Navy mean here? | A very dark blue colour | *The part of a country's armed forces that fights at sea | A type of cake | A small boat on a river
exercise: The Royal Navy and the US Navy are examples of what? | Colours for school jumpers | *Armed forces that fight at sea for their countries | Types of blue paint | Dances from long ago
test: «Her navy skirt matched her school jumper.» What does navy mean in this sentence? | A part of the armed forces | *A very dark blue colour | Something that sails on the sea
test: «In 1588 her navy and stormy weather defeated the Spanish Armada.» What does navy mean here? | A very dark blue colour | A kind of stormy weather | *The ships and sailors that fight at sea
exam: «Ella joined the navy after school, and she loves the sea.» Which meaning of navy is used? | A type of school uniform | *The part of a country's armed forces that fights at sea | A kind of sailing boat | A very dark blue colour
